ckground_tasks.py`** (new): `BackgroundTask` handle and `BackgroundTaskSupervisor` with `add`, `launch_all`, `cancel_all`, and `tasks`. Crashes are logged with their traceback, and cancellation is handled per the spec.\n- **`datasette/app.py`**: supervisor created in `__init__`, plus `add_background_task`, `start_background_tasks`, and `_launch_background_tasks`. Both ASGI wrappers now run `_startup_sequence` and then the launch hook, in that order.\n- **`datasette/cli.py`**: `--get` sets `ds._suppress_background_tasks = True` before the TestClient is built.\n- **`datasette/__init__.py`**: re-exports both classes.\n\nTwo things beyond the letter of the spec:\n- The first version of `cancel_all` never called `task.cancel()`, and one test caught it. I added the cancel call.\n- Cancelling a handle before launch removes it from the list and also frees its name for reuse. The spec only said to remove the handle, so tell me if you'd rather keep the name reserved.\n\nI ran only the four test files the spec lists, not the full suite. `SPEC.md` is still untracked and I didn't commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1381, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 69610, "uuid": "e94f18bb-eeaf-40b0-b5c6-3db81425de4d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1095, "time_to_request_ms": 250, "first_content_frame_ms": 1095, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
